{
  "name": "Nightshade",
  "type": "character",
  "img": "systems/heroic5e/assets/characters/nightshade/Portrait-Nightshade.png",
  "system": {
    "biography": "Evelyn Pike — Nightshade\n\n“The Darkness That Chose Good”\n\nClass: Warden\nOrigin: Monster\nCalling: Redeemer\nSide: Heroic\n\nDescription Nightshade is a deeply troubled young woman bound to a shadow-demon that exists somewhere between possession and symbiosis. The entity grants her terrifying control over darkness and fear, but constantly threatens to overwhelm her emotions and seize control completely. Every use of her powers risks feeding the thing inside her. To the outside world, Nightshade often appears mysterious and frightening, even among other superheroes. Rumors surround her constantly. Some people believe she is cursed. Others think she is barely contained. Both may be true. Despite this, she continues fighting because she refuses to let the darkness define her completely. Personality Intelligent, moody, withdrawn, and emotionally vulnerable beneath her cold exterior. Evelyn struggles with guilt, fear, and isolation, convinced that getting too close to people could eventually endanger them. She often hides pain behind sarcasm or emotional distance, but possesses a deeply compassionate core that occasionally breaks through the shadows. Powers Nightshade controls supernatural shadow energy capable of forming weapons, tendrils, barriers, and living darkness constructs. She can teleport between shadows, project fear, manipulate darkness across entire environments, and partially transform into a far more dangerous demonic form when emotionally overwhelmed.",
    "notes": "Combat Reference\nPower Die: d8\nProwess: +2\nTrained Saves: CON, WIS.\nTrained Skills: Acrobatics, Athletics, Intimidation, Investigation, Occult, Stealth.\nClass & Shadow EV (WIS): 15",
